<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:20:34 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Canada will move faster from US reliance as tariffs take effect and Trump response looms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/canada-will-move-faster-from-us-reliance-as-tariffs-take-effect-and-trump-response-looms</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Tuesday that Canada would move faster to reduce its economic reliance on the United States as retaliatory tariffs took effect on about $20 billion worth of U.S. goods and the country braced for President Donald Trump’s response. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e49123dc-a087-11f1-8dc3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T163056Z-1186857443-RC2R3NAM318W-RTRMADP-3-CANADA-DEFENSE-ICEBREAKERS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e49123dc-a087-11f1-8dc3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T163056Z-1186857443-RC2R3NAM318W-RTRMADP-3-CANADA-DEFENSE-ICEBREAKERS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">128c31f8-abb6-11f1-9f4a-cb5378abc52f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:19:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump tells Putin he wants swift end to Ukraine war, Kremlin says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says</link><description>
US President Donald Trump told Russian President Vladimir Putin he wanted a swift end to the Ukraine war, the Kremlin said, arguing that peace could pave the way for a broad restoration of US-Russia ties. The hour-long call Tuesday followed weekend talks by US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner in Moscow and Kyiv to try to revive stalled peace efforts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ee5ea8d0-abb3-11f1-86a0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4EQ663.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ee5ea8d0-abb3-11f1-86a0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4EQ663.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4fc62874-abb3-11f1-82ac-0768fbfe695b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:07:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ee5ea8d0-abb3-11f1-86a0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4EQ663.jpg">© Jim Watson, Kristina Solovyova, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French police hunt Renoir thieves after lightning museum heist</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-police-hunt-renoir-thieves-after-lightning-museum-heist</link><description>
French police on Tuesday hunted for two thieves who escaped with two Renoir paintings from a museum, after abandoning two others as they fled, in a burglary that reignited concerns about the protection of France's cultural heritage. The heist is the latest in a string of such robberies including the daylight theft last year of crown jewellery valued at around $100 million from the Louvre in Paris. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a0f4a53a-ab5a-11f1-9878-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7M64QY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a0f4a53a-ab5a-11f1-9878-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7M64QY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">872cb72a-abb2-11f1-95e2-636f341c3815</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 18:35:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu under fire over report UAE warned of October 7 attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-under-fire-over-report-uae-warned-of-october-7-attack</link><description>
Israeli opposition leaders on Tuesday called Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu unfit to serve after a report that the United Arab Emirates had warned him before the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack. Haaretz newspaper, in a report excerpted from a forthcoming book by its reporters, said UAE President Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan spoke to Netanyahu a week and a half before the attack and told him that Hamas was planning a major operation. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7332edaa-c267-11f0-9f79-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25319697264730.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7332edaa-c267-11f0-9f79-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25319697264730.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b320344-abb2-11f1-a8eb-0768fbfe695b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 18:31:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UK, France, Canada to ban imports from Israeli settlements</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/uk-france-canada-to-ban-imports-from-israeli-settlements</link><description>
Britain, France and Canada said Tuesday they will ban imports from Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank, with a UK minister accusing Israel of turning a blind eye to the "ethnic cleansing" of Palestinians there. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c018ae48-abaf-11f1-bf07-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4N48XL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c018ae48-abaf-11f1-bf07-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4N48XL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">250b081c-abb2-11f1-825b-636f341c3815</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 18:24:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Missiles or mediation? Trump envoys shuttle between Russia and Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine</link><description>
Exactly two months ago, Ukraine’s momentum was all the talk at a Nato summit in Turkey. What with its long-range drones and Donald Trump’s surprise announcement that the US would allow Kyiv to produce Patriot anti-ballistic missiles on home soil. That was then. This is now: Trump's deal's yet to materialize, Russia’s ramped up cruise missile launches and Ukraine’s run out of air defenses to stop them. Moscow's also failing to stop incoming missiles. What happens in war when for both sides, offense proves better than defense?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8463340a-abae-11f1-890a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T165428Z-1970055042-RC2RDNANYASZ-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-ENVOYS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8463340a-abae-11f1-890a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T165428Z-1970055042-RC2RDNANYASZ-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-ENVOYS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb329508-abaf-11f1-9e7c-0768fbfe695b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 18:19:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Messi, Mbappé and Kane headline Ballon d'Or shortlist, Vozinha named for Yashin award</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260908-messi-mbappe-kane-headline-ballon-d-or-shortlist-vozinha-named-yashin-award</link><description>
Eight-time laureate Lionel Messi is in the 30-man shortlist for the 2026 Men's Ballon ​d'Or, with Harry Kane and Kylian Mbappé among the favourites to succeed France's Ousmane Dembélé. Cape Verde's Vozinha has been shortlisted for the goalkeepers' Yashin Trophy after his heroics at the recent World Cup.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3d9c6f6-aba3-11f1-9216-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L46PB.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3d9c6f6-aba3-11f1-9216-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L46PB.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4993c9e8-aba4-11f1-8352-cb8f382726de</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 17:52:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3d9c6f6-aba3-11f1-9216-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L46PB.jpg">© Franck Fife, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'US Midterm elections tend to be referendums on the unpopularity of the president'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-tend-to-be-referendums-on-the-unpopularity-of-the-president</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome Michelle Swers, Professor of Government at Georgetown University. She frames the New Hampshire primary as both a major Senate contest and an unusually strong indication of the national political climate ahead of November. While Democrats face a difficult Senate map and cannot afford to surrender an open seat they already hold, the broader midterm political environment might become a referendum on President Donald Trump’s performance. New Hampshire is particularly instructive because its closely divided electorate makes national political currents more visible. Swers argues that Trump’s low approval and the local economic consequences of tariffs on Canada create significant headwinds for Republicans, especially in a state whose political identity is strongly associated with resistance to taxation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe2ff40-ab9e-11f1-a32a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-130757-131402-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe2ff40-ab9e-11f1-a32a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-130757-131402-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a565ad1e-ab9e-11f1-9fb0-51605c18cb6e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 16:25:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war</link><description>
Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b728f026-ab9c-11f1-a25d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-211527-212306-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b728f026-ab9c-11f1-a25d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-211527-212306-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd10da6c-ab9c-11f1-ae90-d5d37e7d97b0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 16:16:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>The 'Brenaissance': Brendan Fraser on 'Pressure', winning an Oscar in 'The Whale' and 'The Mummy 4'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260908-the-brenaissance-brendan-fraser-on-pressure-winning-an-oscar-in-the-whale-and-the-mummy-4</link><description>
From "The Mummy" to his Oscar-winning performance in "The Whale", Brendan Fraser's career has taken some extraordinary turns. At the Deauville American Film Festival, he talks to Eve Jackson about his "Brenaissance", playing General Dwight D. Eisenhower in "Pressure", what D-Day can teach us about the dangers of ignoring science and his return as Rick O'Connell in "The Mummy 4".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a278eff6-ab9b-11f1-8814-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5946130736aa02c73443948-11574482.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a278eff6-ab9b-11f1-8814-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5946130736aa02c73443948-11574482.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62af1098-ab9c-11f1-bb89-d5d37e7d97b0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 15:55:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Eve JACKSON</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>World Cup final scorer Torres leads Ballon d'Or nominees</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260908-world-cup-final-scorer-torres-leads-ballon-d-or-nominees</link><description>
Ferran Torres, whose goal against Argentina won the World Cup for Spain in July, leads a 30-man list for the men's Ballon d'Or revealed on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/954a8b72-83bf-11f1-9c28-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/b8d7611554bb33552cf60aa95b29607fbc5c7228.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/954a8b72-83bf-11f1-9c28-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/b8d7611554bb33552cf60aa95b29607fbc5c7228.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff947d22-ab9b-11f1-bad9-51605c18cb6e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 15:43:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/954a8b72-83bf-11f1-9c28-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/b8d7611554bb33552cf60aa95b29607fbc5c7228.jpg">© FRANCK FIFE / AFP</source><dc:creator></dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Eiffel Tower reopens after row over limits on women staff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-eiffel-tower-reopens-after-row-over-limits-on-women-staff</link><description>
The Eiffel Tower reopened Tuesday, a day after one of the world's most-visited landmarks was closed by a strike to protest what a union official called "unacceptable" management instructions limiting the presence of women during a visit by a Hindu religious group close to Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s ruling nationalist party.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b76acdb2-ab96-11f1-bb38-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/minieiffel.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b76acdb2-ab96-11f1-bb38-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/minieiffel.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7435418e-ab97-11f1-ad2a-d5d37e7d97b0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 15:18:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Israel to close British consulate in Jerusalem after sanctions on settlements</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-israel-to-close-british-consulate-in-jerusalem-after-sanctions-on-settlements</link><description>
British Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband accused the Israeli government on Tuesday of turning a "blind eye" to what he called "ethnic cleansing" by settlers in the West Bank as the UK joined France and ten other countries in banning imports from Israeli settlements in the occupied territory. The decision comes amid rising violence over settlement expansion. Follow our liveblog for the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d0aaf1c-ab95-11f1-bf19-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4N84NZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d0aaf1c-ab95-11f1-bf19-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4N84NZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">86758a44-ab96-11f1-88c6-d5d37e7d97b0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 15:10:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d0aaf1c-ab95-11f1-bf19-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4N84NZ.jpg">© Ahmad Gharabli, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France joins ban on products from Israeli settlements in West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-france-joins-ban-on-products-from-israeli-settlements-in-west-bank</link><description>
France will join the UK and other countries in launching a process to ban products from Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël ​Barrot said on Tuesday, amid rising settler violence that has further undermined prospects for a two-state solution with the Palestinians. France 24's Marc Perelman has the details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9bc0be0-ab92-11f1-8ba9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-160715-161105-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9bc0be0-ab92-11f1-8ba9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-160715-161105-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef183b5e-ab92-11f1-87a4-d5f57f4dde63</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:48:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UK ban on goods from Israeli settlements 'evidence of Netanyahu's failure'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-uk-ban-on-goods-from-israeli-settlements-evidence-of-natanyahu-s-failure</link><description>
British foreign minister Ed Miliband accused the Israeli government on Tuesday of turning a "blind eye" to what he called "ethnic cleansing" by settlers in the West Bank. Miliband told parliament the UK government would introduce "an import ban on goods from illegal settlements in the occupied territories", in a move coordinated with other countries. Jordana Miller, ABC correspondent in Jerusalem, told France 24 that the ban was evidence of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu to rein in the far-right elements of his government that has facilitated the growth of settlements.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e391a06-ab91-11f1-b5d5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-160221-160711-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e391a06-ab91-11f1-b5d5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-160221-160711-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a2eca630-ab91-11f1-a96e-8f413afe3879</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:47:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴Israel to shut down UK consulate in Jerusalem in response to sanctions on settlements</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-france-and-canada-to-join-uk-in-banning-goods-from-israeli-west-bank-settlements</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">a466c962-ab93-11f1-80aa-2734c8b3e324</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:45:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Eiffel Tower reopens after row over removing women staff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-eiffel-tower-reopens-after-row-over-removing-women-staff</link><description>
The Eiffel Tower reopened on Tuesday after staff walked out over the removal of women colleagues during a visit by a Hindu religious group which later apologised. The operating company that runs the Paris landmark, SETE, acknowledged that the Hindu delegation had requested the visit on Saturday be organised so as to limit "interactions with women" and said that "these conditions should not have been accepted".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5fe3fca-ab8e-11f1-b1b8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-153614-153757-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5fe3fca-ab8e-11f1-b1b8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-153614-153757-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">baba0184-ab8e-11f1-a523-d5f57f4dde63</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:38:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Sounding the fire alarm: Why French firefighters are going on strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260908-sounding-the-fire-alarm-why-french-firefighters-are-going-on-strike</link><description>
We dive into the particularities of France's firefighting system, including how they came to be called "sapeurs-pompiers", this as firefighters kick off six weeks of strikes. Finally, we discuss how other public service workers are also calling for industrial action.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0601cae-ab8a-11f1-bbf8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-697932066aa0100555e277-14469226.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0601cae-ab8a-11f1-bbf8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-697932066aa0100555e277-14469226.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07e971cc-ab8c-11f1-bd1a-d5f57f4dde63</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:12:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Solange MOUGIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spoiler alert: AI in cinema 'just a tool, won’t replace actors and human beings'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-spoiler-alert-ai-in-cinema-just-a-tool-won-t-replace-actors-and-human-beings-1</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome film producer Lahoucine Grimich. He challenges the prevailing narrative that cinema is an industry in existential crisis. While acknowledging that viewing habits have dramatically shifted since the pandemic, he argues that streaming platforms, public support and theatrical exhibition are not competing forces. As demonstrated in the French model, they form parts of an interconnected financing ecosystem in which cinema can adapt without ever abandoning the big screen. He frames filmmaking as a form of cultural sovereignty: societies need films not simply as entertainment, but to recognise themselves and to create what he calls “new imaginaries.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ffeb164-ab86-11f1-8ddf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-081209-081733-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ffeb164-ab86-11f1-8ddf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-081209-081733-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37cce99c-ab86-11f1-9bb5-637ae701f8ef</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:11:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New Hampshire voters pick 2026 midterm candidates</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-new-hampshire-voters-pick-2026-midterm-candidates</link><description>
A late surge by a progressive challenger has injected drama into New Hampshire's Democratic Senate primary on Tuesday, threatening to complicate US Representative Chris Pappas' path to nomination. In one of the last states holding primaries in 2026, New Hampshire voters will also choose nominees in a Republican Senate primary and in primaries for two US House seats, just eight weeks before the November 3 general election when control of Congress is at stake. France 24's Fraser Jackson has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/acbbd1de-ab89-11f1-bed5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-141004-141417-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/acbbd1de-ab89-11f1-bed5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-141004-141417-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b324f942-ab89-11f1-a270-8398847d1e73</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 13:47:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'The age of cultural resurgence': Africa's mother tongues finding new life</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-the-age-of-cultural-resurgence-africa-s-mother-tongues-finding-new-life</link><description>
Across the African continent, indigenous languages, once marginalised under colonial rule, are seeing renewed interest from younger generations, especially in the diaspora. Modern technology is providing them with new ways to reconnect with their heritage and older generations of their families. Clemence Waller reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77a3d9c0-ab88-11f1-90c8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-225230-225405-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77a3d9c0-ab88-11f1-90c8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-225230-225405-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d3a3988-ab88-11f1-b560-8398847d1e73</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 13:46:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who is Sarah Khalifa, the Egyptian TV presenter sentenced to death?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-who-is-sarah-khalifa-the-egyptian-tv-presenter-sentenced-to-death</link><description>
An Egyptian court has sentenced a well-known television presenter and 11 others to death for manufacturing and trafficking narcotics in a sprawling drugs case. The presenter, Sarah Khalifa, 39, is best known for her program "Mission Impossible", which dealt with issues concerning security and crime.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/486eb288-ab88-11f1-89dc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-224844-225013-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/486eb288-ab88-11f1-89dc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-224844-225013-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d3cccf0-ab88-11f1-925d-8398847d1e73</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 13:44:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UK, France and ten other countries to sanction trade from Israeli settlements</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-uk-france-and-ten-other-countries-to-sanction-trade-from-israeli-settlements</link><description>
Twelve countries including Britain, Canada and France Tuesday said they would slap sanctions on trade with Israeli settlements in the West Bank, after increasing attacks by Israeli settlers against Palestinian villages in the occupied territory. British Foreign Minister Ed ​Miliband said Britain ‌could no longer simply "call out" injustice and suffering, but told the House of Commons that the country now had ⁠to "act" to oppose the expansion of settlements.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ee15d70-ab8a-11f1-8a39-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-150111-150530-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ee15d70-ab8a-11f1-8a39-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-150111-150530-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6451c0ce-ab8a-11f1-9738-637ae701f8ef</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 13:42:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Be kind with yourself': US expat Robin Allison Davis on surviving cancer in Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260908-be-kind-to-yourself-us-expat-robin-allison-davis-on-surviving-cancer-in-paris</link><description>
An American woman who moved to Paris and soon afterwards was twice diagnosed with breast cancer has spoken to FRANCE 24 about how she managed to get through the trauma. The paperback version of Robin Allison Davis's book "Surviving Paris: A Memoir of Healing in the City of Light" has just come out. The reviews say it's full of sorrow, laughter and some unforgettable cringeworthy moments. Davis told us the only way to survive in her situation was to be kind to herself, admitting that she did a lot of writing and crying at the same time. She spoke to us in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44217c8e-ab82-11f1-9844-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-127509746aa001e3a65227-91985227.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44217c8e-ab82-11f1-9844-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-127509746aa001e3a65227-91985227.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d54b1c5e-ab70-11f1-8520-c73627a799d4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 13:21:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
